WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:03.920
WRITTEN BY HYUGA NATSU

01:32.050 --> 01:33.426
THIS STORY IS A FICTION AND ALL NAMES OF
FIGURES AND ORGANIZATIONS ARE FICTITIOUS.

01:33.510 --> 01:34.886
MOREOVER, THE STORY HAS NO RELATION
TO REAL-LIFE INCIDENTS AND EVENTS.

01:37.597 --> 01:40.183
-I'm going to the Jade Pavilion.
-Yes.

01:42.977 --> 01:44.103
She has passed away?

01:45.104 --> 01:46.105
&lrm;I see.

01:46.898 --> 01:47.982
Lady Jin has?

01:48.066 --> 01:51.444
It seems to have been food poisoning.
The report just came in.

01:52.779 --> 01:56.324
I had heard she was bedridden
this past year, but…

01:59.994 --> 02:01.955
Lord Jinshi has arrived.

02:02.831 --> 02:04.290
Let him through, please.

02:05.959 --> 02:07.210
Please do these.

02:07.293 --> 02:08.419
Of course.

02:13.174 --> 02:14.592
<i>I shouldn't interrupt.</i>

02:15.552 --> 02:17.470
A palace woman has gone missing?

02:17.554 --> 02:20.431
Yes, that's right. Her name is Tao.

02:20.515 --> 02:23.393
She was a hardworking
and earnest young lady.

02:23.476 --> 02:25.436
Just as her term of service was ending…

02:25.520 --> 02:27.522
and her wedding was approaching too.

02:28.189 --> 02:29.399
Wedding, you say?

02:29.482 --> 02:32.443
I heard she was given
a hairpin at the garden party.

02:32.527 --> 02:36.990
And it was from a promising civil servant
with good prospects.

02:37.073 --> 02:39.450
It seems the palace supervisor
was holding her back.

02:39.534 --> 02:41.536
Eh?

02:41.619 --> 02:43.454
<i>So, such an excellent palace woman</i>

02:43.538 --> 02:47.041
<i>disappears without a word,</i>
<i>even though her wedding was near?</i>

02:49.460 --> 02:51.880
Do you have any idea what happened?

02:51.963 --> 02:54.257
I have no idea.

02:54.340 --> 02:57.093
Well, it’s not like
it’s completely unheard of.

02:57.802 --> 03:00.805
<i>A lot of the women struggle with</i>
<i>interpersonal relationships.</i>

03:00.889 --> 03:01.848
<i>Indeed.</i>

03:04.517 --> 03:07.270
<i>Sometimes, when I'm here like this,</i>
<i>I almost forget that…</i>

03:08.146 --> 03:09.898
<i>this is the rear palace,</i>

03:09.981 --> 03:13.192
<i>a garden where 2,000 women</i>
<i>stir and scheme.</i>

03:17.155 --> 03:18.698
<i>Today, there's a tea party outside.</i>

03:19.407 --> 03:21.951
<i>If they stay up too long,</i>
<i>people might suspect pregnancy.</i>

03:22.744 --> 03:24.871
<i>They're mindful of the location</i>
<i>and their attire,</i>

03:24.954 --> 03:27.874
<i>but by now, some must have noticed.</i>

03:27.957 --> 03:31.044
<i>The real question is whether</i>
<i>those who've noticed are harmful…</i>

03:31.127 --> 03:32.795
<i>or harmless.</i>

03:32.879 --> 03:34.297
Oh, you're back.

03:36.841 --> 03:39.052
Maomao, over here.

03:43.223 --> 03:44.641
Did you call for me?

03:44.724 --> 03:46.976
No, but he did.

03:47.977 --> 03:50.313
Shall we change the location?

03:51.064 --> 03:53.191
There's no particular problem here.

03:53.274 --> 03:54.817
Why don't we talk here?

03:55.443 --> 03:59.781
No, I can't stay too long
at the Consort's side.

03:59.864 --> 04:01.157
And besides, do you hear that?

04:03.743 --> 04:07.538
-Oh.
-Please, Your Highness, give up.

04:10.833 --> 04:13.127
So, what is it you need?

04:13.878 --> 04:18.883
You know the Emperor has been
handing out novels to his consorts lately.

04:18.967 --> 04:22.887
Yes. And after they read them,
the attendants read them as well,

04:22.971 --> 04:25.890
<i>and it seems like they're reading them</i>
<i>aloud to the other palace women.</i>

04:27.058 --> 04:27.892
<i>Copies are being circulated,</i>

04:27.976 --> 04:30.687
and some are even
trying to learn how to read.

04:30.770 --> 04:32.063
I see.

04:33.398 --> 04:35.692
Though it's still in the conceptual stage,

04:35.775 --> 04:38.695
I was thinking of making
something like this.

04:38.778 --> 04:41.948
I believe they call it a "writing school"
among commoners.

04:42.031 --> 04:44.617
<i>A school for the maidservants, huh?</i>

04:44.701 --> 04:46.953
<i>I had a feeling he was up to something,</i>

04:47.036 --> 04:49.205
<i>but he is surprisingly quick to act.</i>

04:50.456 --> 04:51.291
It's a good idea.

04:51.374 --> 04:52.750
What?!

04:52.834 --> 04:55.003
What happened to your usual gaze?!

04:55.086 --> 04:57.505
Is something wrong with your health?

04:57.588 --> 04:59.132
What’s with that reaction?

04:59.799 --> 05:02.385
No, it's just that I feel uneasy…

05:06.306 --> 05:07.181
<i>Masochists.</i>

05:09.976 --> 05:11.811
So, what do you think?

05:11.894 --> 05:15.648
Actually, there are those who wish
to learn, so I think it’s a fine idea.

05:16.566 --> 05:19.360
It will also connect to work
after their apprenticeship ends.

05:19.444 --> 05:20.403
I see.

05:21.195 --> 05:23.364
-But…
-Go ahead and say it.

05:24.240 --> 05:25.700
The southern side…

05:25.783 --> 05:28.411
while it’s convenient for deliveries
and such, it’s near the main gate

05:28.494 --> 05:32.248
and a prime spot for the senior
and middle-ranking consorts.

05:32.332 --> 05:35.084
<i>Many of them are very proud.</i>

05:35.168 --> 05:37.462
<i>They may not feel comfortable</i>

05:37.545 --> 05:39.589
<i>about the maidservants being educated.</i>

05:40.965 --> 05:43.092
It's better to move it
to the northern side then.

05:43.176 --> 05:46.721
Yes. That area is less maintained,

05:46.804 --> 05:49.307
and there are even unused buildings.

05:49.932 --> 05:52.143
If we renovate that, it should be enough.

05:52.769 --> 05:57.273
Also, how about presenting it as
vocational training on the surface?

05:57.356 --> 06:00.359
If people view it as a means to
make a living, more will gather.

06:01.569 --> 06:02.695
Is that so?

06:02.779 --> 06:05.656
Perhaps try giving them
snacks occasionally.

06:05.740 --> 06:06.741
Occasionally?

06:06.824 --> 06:10.203
Yes. An occasional treat
is the most effective.

06:11.120 --> 06:12.622
I see.

06:13.706 --> 06:18.336
<i>The idea isn’t bad, but his upbringing</i>
<i>makes his execution weak.</i>

06:18.419 --> 06:21.130
<i>I'm sure he's asking</i>
<i>because he's aware of it too.</i>

06:21.214 --> 06:23.633
This is just
my subjective opinion, though.

06:24.842 --> 06:26.511
Is that all you wanted to talk about?

06:26.594 --> 06:29.013
Ah. And one more thing.

06:29.097 --> 06:31.349
Are you familiar with mushrooms?

06:32.517 --> 06:37.105
Well, I use them both for food
and medicine, so I know a bit.

06:37.188 --> 06:39.148
Around this time of year,

06:39.232 --> 06:43.361
there are always palace women who pick
mushrooms and end up with food poisoning.

06:43.444 --> 06:46.405
There’s always someone
who’s too greedy for food.

06:46.489 --> 06:51.452
Exactly. There was someone at the
medical office eating <i>matsutake</i> mushrooms.

06:51.536 --> 06:54.455
I’ve heard that the fruit
from the orchard also tends to disappear.

06:55.081 --> 06:57.416
<i>Those were not poisonous mushrooms.</i>

06:57.500 --> 07:00.753
<i>As for the orchard,</i>
<i>I was just pruning and tasting them.</i>

07:00.837 --> 07:05.216
So, please dispose of anything
that could be mistakenly eaten.

07:05.299 --> 07:08.594
Also, let me know what kind of
poisonous mushrooms there are.

07:09.387 --> 07:13.433
At the Jade Pavilion, you'll mainly rest,
except for poison testing.

07:15.351 --> 07:19.981
<i>If that's the case, isn't it better</i>
<i>to explain it in front of Lady Gyokuyou?</i>

07:22.275 --> 07:24.318
<i>What’s going on with him?</i>

07:25.778 --> 07:27.155
I’m counting on you.

07:27.864 --> 07:29.157
Understood.

07:29.240 --> 07:33.661
<i>There might be something behind all this,</i>
<i>but it sounds interesting.</i>

07:35.538 --> 07:38.040
<i>Now, where should I start?</i>

07:38.708 --> 07:41.169
<i>The garden, the orchard, the pine forest…</i>

07:41.252 --> 07:44.630
<i>There are many places</i>
<i>where mushrooms might grow.</i>

07:44.714 --> 07:46.966
<i>It’s the season when</i>
<i>they’re sprouting everywhere.</i>

07:47.925 --> 07:51.721
<i>If the palace women are picking them</i>
<i>secretly, places where people often go</i>

07:51.804 --> 07:54.682
<i>or the southern side</i>
<i>can probably be excluded.</i>

07:56.058 --> 07:59.103
<i>So, if that's the case…</i>
<i>it’s probably towards the north.</i>

08:11.782 --> 08:15.620
<i>What is this smell?</i>
<i>It’s strangely pungent…</i>

08:17.830 --> 08:21.125
<i>Is this the weird smell</i>
<i>that Shisui mentioned before?</i>

08:21.209 --> 08:23.669
<i>Maybe the leaked sewage</i>
<i>is acting as nutrients,</i>

08:23.753 --> 08:26.214
<i>and that’s why the mushrooms</i>
<i>are growing so well.</i>

08:28.132 --> 08:29.509
I’m back. I’ve returned.

08:30.301 --> 08:32.386
Welcome back!

08:34.639 --> 08:36.349
Don’t come in all dirty!

08:36.432 --> 08:37.475
<i>Dirty…</i>

08:37.558 --> 08:41.103
Maomao, you smell!
What on earth were you doing?

08:42.063 --> 08:45.066
It was a very fulfilling day.

08:45.816 --> 08:48.569
<i>I managed to harvest some mushrooms</i>
<i>that can be used as medicine.</i>

08:49.278 --> 08:53.491
<i>I told the quack doctor that they're</i>
<i>poisonous, so he won’t eat them.</i>

08:54.825 --> 08:59.163
It’s almost time for Lady Gyokuyou’s
evening meal, so please change quickly.

08:59.247 --> 09:00.081
Yes.

09:03.251 --> 09:05.711
Excuse me. I’m sorry for being late.

09:08.130 --> 09:09.840
I apologize for rushing you.

09:10.466 --> 09:11.342
No.

09:12.009 --> 09:15.137
<i>The black cords on their wrists…</i>

09:16.305 --> 09:20.601
I’ll be going out after the evening meal.
Please come with me.

09:20.685 --> 09:21.602
Understood.

09:22.812 --> 09:27.108
<i>In other words, someone of noble status</i>
<i>in the rear palace has passed away.</i>

09:30.695 --> 09:33.322
She was a consort named Jin.

09:33.406 --> 09:35.616
She's one of
the top intermediate consorts.

09:36.284 --> 09:37.702
Daughter of a high official.

09:38.369 --> 09:42.665
For the past year, she had been unwell
and confined to her quarters.

09:42.748 --> 09:46.210
It seems she suffered from food poisoning,
and that was the end.

09:46.294 --> 09:49.922
The Emperor never visited her;

09:50.006 --> 09:52.133
she should have returned
to her family home.

09:53.551 --> 09:57.430
That’s unusual. It’s rare for you
to speak so harshly.

10:01.017 --> 10:03.436
Lady Jin was a bit…

10:03.519 --> 10:06.314
She was someone
with a rather difficult personality.

10:06.397 --> 10:09.108
She was intensely jealous
of other consorts and maidservants.

10:09.859 --> 10:13.362
<i>She would spread slander and resort to</i>
<i>violence against those of lower status…</i>

10:14.071 --> 10:18.159
It was around that time
when Lady Gyokuyou, who was pregnant

10:18.242 --> 10:19.619
with the princess, was poisoned.

10:22.204 --> 10:27.084
Of course, she wouldn’t directly harass
the higher-ranking consorts.

10:27.168 --> 10:30.671
But, with a personality like that…

10:30.755 --> 10:34.592
It seems that Lord Jinshi
inquired about the situation.

10:34.675 --> 10:36.093
<i>But…</i>

10:37.428 --> 10:40.181
Is there any evidence?

10:41.807 --> 10:45.144
In the end, it remained mere suspicion.

10:45.227 --> 10:47.271
Things got quite chaotic internally,

10:47.355 --> 10:48.814
and even her attendants…

10:48.898 --> 10:52.777
suffered from the fallout. Honestly,

10:53.486 --> 10:55.696
I can’t help but feel relieved
it ended like this.

10:55.780 --> 10:58.449
If anything had happened to
Lady Gyokuyou again…

11:01.327 --> 11:04.747
<i>For Miss Hongniang,</i>
<i>that's her honest feelings.</i>

11:06.040 --> 11:08.626
It seems she suffered food poisoning
and passed away.

11:08.709 --> 11:12.046
Also, let me know what kind of
poisonous mushrooms there are.

11:13.047 --> 11:17.009
<i>Why would Lord Jinshi ask me</i>
<i>to investigate mushrooms?</i>

11:17.885 --> 11:22.681
<i>Why didn’t they talk about this in the</i>
<i>Jade Pavilion where Lady Gyokuyou resides?</i>

11:22.765 --> 11:27.186
<i>It’s because they suspect someone</i>
<i>from the Jade Pavilion.</i>

11:27.853 --> 11:30.773
<i>Of being the one who killed Lady Jin</i>
<i>with poisonous mushrooms.</i>

11:31.649 --> 11:35.069
<i>Although it seemed they were</i>
<i>overly partial to Lady Gyokuyou,</i>

11:35.152 --> 11:37.530
<i>they’re actually handling</i>
<i>things fairly, aren’t they?</i>

11:38.364 --> 11:40.825
<i>But if their true intentions were exposed,</i>

11:40.908 --> 11:43.536
<i>it would surely affect</i>
<i>trust in the future.</i>

11:44.453 --> 11:48.082
<i>However, Lady Gyokuyou is unlikely</i>
<i>to be the culprit.</i>

11:48.165 --> 11:50.292
<i>Poisoning someone to death</i>
<i>is too labor-intensive,</i>

11:50.376 --> 11:53.963
<i>and there are countless other ways</i>
<i>to bring down a mid-ranking concubine.</i>

11:54.046 --> 11:57.716
<i>As for the other attendants, they aren’t</i>
<i>suited for such covert operations.</i>

11:57.800 --> 12:00.469
<i>If that’s the case, the one suspected is…</i>

12:01.220 --> 12:02.888
Me, huh?

12:02.972 --> 12:04.974
<i>If asking me to search</i>
<i>for poisonous mushrooms</i>

12:05.057 --> 12:07.935
<i>was a way to gauge my reaction,</i>

12:08.018 --> 12:10.563
<i>I can’t help but feel impressed</i>
<i>rather than disappointed.</i>

12:11.480 --> 12:12.398
&lrm;Please.

12:14.275 --> 12:15.151
&lrm;Huh?

12:15.234 --> 12:19.155
<i>She's Lady Jin's attendant.</i>
<i>Did she develop a rash from something?</i>

12:19.905 --> 12:22.116
-Here you are.
-<i>But, that wound…</i>

12:27.538 --> 12:30.207
<i>If only I could’ve known</i>
<i>what symptoms she had</i>

12:30.291 --> 12:32.251
<i>while she was alive.</i>

12:44.346 --> 12:46.974
Lady Sou! Please stop!

13:02.573 --> 13:04.533
It’s her own fault.

13:06.452 --> 13:08.370
<i>That blistered face…</i>

13:08.454 --> 13:10.706
Are you familiar with mushrooms?

13:10.789 --> 13:14.585
Even her attendants
suffered from the fallout.

13:16.295 --> 13:18.047
<i>I see, it’s all starting to make sense.</i>

13:19.673 --> 13:22.343
<i>The thing Lord Jinshi was searching for…</i>

13:27.056 --> 13:28.891
<i>The woman who caused the scene yesterday,</i>

13:28.974 --> 13:31.810
<i>I heard she was</i>
<i>a low-ranked consort named Sou.</i>

13:31.894 --> 13:34.146
<i>Daughter of a wealthy merchant family,</i>
<i>good-natured,</i>

13:34.939 --> 13:38.108
<i>and the Emperor would occasionally</i>
<i>visit her chambers.</i>

13:38.192 --> 13:41.153
<i>However, around this time two years ago…</i>

13:43.239 --> 13:46.283
Why… how could this happen?!

13:47.076 --> 13:51.080
<i>She contracted a mysterious illness and</i>
<i>was dropped from the consort's position.</i>

13:51.163 --> 13:55.584
<i>But, even if she returned to her family,</i>
<i>she would no longer be able to marry.</i>

13:56.252 --> 13:59.588
<i>Keeping her in the rear palace</i>
<i>must have been the Emperor's kindness.</i>

14:01.674 --> 14:04.218
<i>So then, why did</i>
<i>that lower-ranking consort</i>

14:04.301 --> 14:06.595
<i>do such a thing at Lady Jin’s funeral?</i>

14:06.679 --> 14:08.681
<i>The answer is simple.</i>

14:08.764 --> 14:12.476
<i>She believed that the cause of</i>
<i>her illness was Lady Jin.</i>

14:16.438 --> 14:17.356
<i>Found it.</i>

14:21.944 --> 14:23.404
Lord Jinshi, take a look at this.

14:24.238 --> 14:25.948
How ominous.

14:26.031 --> 14:27.908
Yes, it's highly poisonous.

14:40.212 --> 14:42.631
This… where did you find it?

14:43.257 --> 14:45.092
In the northern wooded area.

14:45.175 --> 14:47.720
It seems the overgrown,
neglected forest provided

14:47.803 --> 14:50.639
a good environment for this mushroom.

14:50.723 --> 14:53.601
Although its occurrence is rare,

14:53.684 --> 14:55.936
it’s an extremely dangerous specimen.

14:56.020 --> 14:59.481
Even a tiny fragment ingested
is enough to reach a lethal dose,

14:59.565 --> 15:03.485
and just touching it releases toxicity.
Please don’t get any closer.

15:03.569 --> 15:06.113
You’ll end up like Lady Jin
or Lady Sou if you do.

15:09.867 --> 15:14.622
Long ago, I found these mushrooms
while gathering herbs with my father…

15:14.705 --> 15:16.749
-Did you touch it?
-Yes.

15:16.832 --> 15:19.460
I washed it off immediately,
but as you can see, this is the result.

15:20.628 --> 15:23.714
Are there still marks under that bandage?

15:23.797 --> 15:27.301
No, the rest are scars
from my own experiments.

15:27.384 --> 15:29.094
Wait, what kind of experiments?

15:29.178 --> 15:31.347
-It's… a hobby.
-A hobby? What kind of hobby?

15:31.972 --> 15:34.350
<i>I've never shown it to anyone before.</i>

15:34.433 --> 15:37.978
-Well, that's not important right now.
-Not important…?

15:39.313 --> 15:41.106
The body of Lady Jin that at the funeral

15:41.190 --> 15:44.109
<i>had blistered skin and hair loss.</i>

15:44.818 --> 15:49.406
Weren't you investigating
the source of this poison?

15:49.490 --> 15:51.200
As sharp as ever.

15:54.161 --> 15:57.623
Two years ago, Lady Sou suddenly
fell ill with a mysterious disease.

15:57.706 --> 16:00.417
It was suspected
that poison was the cause.

16:00.501 --> 16:02.503
And the person rumored
to be the culprit was…

16:03.379 --> 16:05.547
-Lady Jin.
-That's right.

16:06.298 --> 16:10.552
But there was no conclusive evidence
to prove that she administered the poison.

16:10.636 --> 16:11.804
And then, a year ago…

16:12.888 --> 16:16.558
<i>Lady Jin started exhibiting</i>
<i>the same symptoms as Lady Sou.</i>

16:16.642 --> 16:20.312
<i>She must have accidentally touched</i>
<i>the poison while using it on someone else.</i>

16:21.063 --> 16:24.775
After that, Lady Jin became depressed
and was like a different person.

16:25.985 --> 16:31.031
<i>I visited to check on her once a month,</i>
<i>but she was barely able to speak.</i>

16:31.949 --> 16:34.827
She was a proud
and dignified consort to begin with.

16:34.910 --> 16:37.204
Unable to bear it, she poisoned herself…

16:37.287 --> 16:41.125
That’s the testimony of the serving maids
who attended her.

16:41.792 --> 16:45.421
<i>At first glance,</i>
<i>it seems to make sense. But…</i>

16:46.255 --> 16:49.174
Lady Jin died after ingesting
a poisonous mushroom, didn’t she?

16:49.258 --> 16:52.469
-Yes.
-Then there’s something odd about that.

16:53.095 --> 16:54.888
What do you mean?

16:55.472 --> 16:57.182
This mushroom, when eaten,

16:57.266 --> 17:00.227
causes stomach pain,
vomiting, and numbness.

17:00.310 --> 17:03.313
It also causes inflammation in the mouth,

17:03.397 --> 17:05.816
but I’ve never heard of
it spreading to the face.

17:05.899 --> 17:07.067
Is that true?

17:07.693 --> 17:12.656
Yes. The swelling on the face
looked quite recent.

17:12.740 --> 17:16.285
It was as if the poisonous mushroom
had been directly rubbed onto her face.

17:16.368 --> 17:19.246
<i>Meanwhile, her hands</i>
<i>remained perfectly clean.</i>

17:19.329 --> 17:20.539
<i>The body part with blisters was…</i>

17:25.169 --> 17:27.379
If you have something to say,
go ahead and say it.

17:33.260 --> 17:34.720
Could you give me a few days?

17:35.429 --> 17:40.017
If possible, could you provide
a few capable and tight-lipped eunuchs?

17:41.560 --> 17:43.479
I’m not sure, but…

17:44.188 --> 17:45.064
Still, do it.

17:46.857 --> 17:50.069
<i>Well, being ordered around</i>
<i>is probably easier for me.</i>

17:51.320 --> 17:52.654
Understood.

17:55.532 --> 17:59.828
But what is Xiaomao planning
to investigate?

17:59.912 --> 18:01.455
I don’t know.

18:01.538 --> 18:02.706
But…

18:02.790 --> 18:07.169
The apothecary's job in such times
is simply to search for evidence.

18:27.356 --> 18:28.357
We've arrived.

18:30.651 --> 18:31.819
Mushrooms…

18:32.528 --> 18:34.571
Could you dig here?

18:34.655 --> 18:35.531
Understood.

18:47.709 --> 18:48.877
This smell…

19:01.765 --> 19:03.892
Is this the evidence?

19:04.560 --> 19:07.896
I didn’t expect to get it right
on the first try.

19:09.773 --> 19:13.527
That body, it seems to be Lady Jin's.

19:13.610 --> 19:15.737
Her family crest was on the ornaments.

19:16.363 --> 19:18.866
Whether it was murder or an accident,
we can't be sure, but…

19:18.949 --> 19:21.702
she must have died a year ago.

19:21.785 --> 19:23.954
Was it around the time she fell ill?

19:24.037 --> 19:26.582
Yes. The real one was buried
in the forest,

19:26.665 --> 19:29.543
<i>and I believe someone else took her place.</i>

19:29.626 --> 19:32.212
So, what about the body at the funeral?

19:33.547 --> 19:35.716
Do you know of the missing palace woman?

19:36.633 --> 19:40.804
A woman named Tao,
who disappeared before her marriage.

19:41.555 --> 19:43.724
She looks very similar to
Lady Jin, doesn't she?

19:44.975 --> 19:48.228
<i>From the inquiries I made,</i>
<i>it seems their build was quite similar.</i>

19:48.937 --> 19:52.024
<i>If her face was covered,</i>
<i>the only ones who could identify her</i>

19:52.107 --> 19:53.734
<i>would probably be her attendants.</i>

19:54.318 --> 19:58.363
It would have been possible
to deceive those who came once a month.

19:58.447 --> 19:59.573
In other words,

19:59.656 --> 20:03.619
that woman, Tao, conspired together
with Lady Jin's attendants?

20:03.702 --> 20:07.331
Probably, I don’t know
the exact details, but…

20:10.834 --> 20:12.711
<i>I have my own assumptions.</i>

20:13.378 --> 20:14.963
<i>The trigger was likely jealousy.</i>

20:15.047 --> 20:20.177
<i>Lady Jin didn't like that a palace</i>
<i>woman resembling her was being courted.</i>

20:21.053 --> 20:24.973
<i>She resented the fact</i>
<i>that the Emperor never visited her.</i>

20:25.057 --> 20:28.977
<i>In fact, it seems</i>
<i>Tao was being treated terribly.</i>

20:29.061 --> 20:31.188
<i>Perhaps that led to a quarrel,</i>

20:31.271 --> 20:33.982
<i>whether it was murder</i>
<i>or an accident, Lady Jin died.</i>

20:34.733 --> 20:37.778
<i>The attendants, perhaps out of</i>
<i>self-preservation and sympathy for Tao,</i>

20:37.861 --> 20:40.739
<i>proposed to cover up Lady Jin's death.</i>

20:40.822 --> 20:42.741
<i>Tao could hardly refuse.</i>

20:43.617 --> 20:47.079
<i>But as the discussion for marriage</i>
<i>progressed,</i>

20:47.162 --> 20:50.249
<i>it became impossible</i>
<i>to continue the deception.</i>

20:53.752 --> 20:55.045
<i>Yeah, I should stop.</i>

20:55.128 --> 20:58.298
<i>The motive can be created by</i>
<i>the high-ranking officials as they please.</i>

20:58.382 --> 21:02.886
However, how did you know
where the body was buried?

21:02.970 --> 21:06.265
-There was evidence left behind.
-Evidence?

21:08.350 --> 21:09.268
Mushrooms!

21:09.351 --> 21:11.853
The mushrooms growing around there
prefer to grow near

21:11.937 --> 21:14.523
animal carcasses and feces.

21:14.606 --> 21:17.442
No wonder there was
a distinct rotten smell.

21:17.526 --> 21:21.488
I never imagined I was observing
mushrooms on top of a corpse…

21:24.241 --> 21:26.243
What are you going to do
with those mushrooms?

21:29.371 --> 21:31.790
There are many very interesting
mushrooms in here.

21:31.873 --> 21:33.583
Mushrooms that grow on corpses?

21:33.667 --> 21:37.671
I haven't found any mushrooms
like caterpillar fungus.

21:38.588 --> 21:41.466
Also, if it grows on humans,
it would be human fungus.

21:41.550 --> 21:42.676
Take it away!

21:50.267 --> 21:52.853
<i>It was just pure curiosity…</i>

22:00.694 --> 22:03.238
<i>Mushrooms that grow from corpses, huh?</i>

22:06.158 --> 22:07.743
<i>If they exist…</i>

22:08.994 --> 22:10.412
<i>what form would they take?</i>

22:11.330 --> 22:13.665
<i>And what properties would they have?</i>

23:46.049 --> 23:49.970
NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW

23:57.394 --> 23:59.771
<i>The next episode is "Replica."</i>

24:00.981 --> 24:01.815
